FINAL ANSWER:
The git history can show who wrote and last touched each file. It can't show who is still around. I only have commit dates to go on, so treat "active" below as "committed recently".

**Official review routing**

`CODEOWNERS` sends everything to `@google/go-uuid-contributors`, with no per-file owners. I can't see that team's membership from the repo, so check it on GitHub.

**Who wrote each part**

| Area | Original author (most of the code today) | Recent maintainers |
|---|---|---|
| `time.go` | Paul Borman wrote about 111 lines (10 commits, 2016) | Alexander Rowe (2025-02), Sam Okafor (2025-04), Nicu Micle (2024-11), MikeWang (2023-11) |
| `version7.go` | MikeWang wrote about 101 lines (2024-01) | Mei Chen (2025-08, added `Time7`), Ravi Menon (2026-05, v7 clock step-back docs) |
| SQL (`database_sql.go`, formerly `sql.go`) | Justin Overfelt wrote the most lines (2015). Also David E. Wheeler, Andrew Stone, "thehazard" | Ravi Menon (2025-03), Steven Kaufman (2021) |

There is no `sql.go` any more. It was renamed to `database_sql.go`, and `git log --follow` recovers the history.

**Are the original authors still around?**

- **Paul Borman:** probably not. His last commit is 2023-10-26, and he wrote most of the library. He is the person to ask about `time.go` if you can reach him.
- **MikeWang:** probably not. His last commit is 2024-07, and he wrote nearly all of `version7.go`.
- **Justin Overfelt, David E. Wheeler, Andrew Stone:** none has committed to the SQL code since 2017, and Wheeler's last was 2016.
- **Active in the last year:** Ravi Menon (latest commit 2026-06-17, touches all three areas), Alexander Rowe, Mei Chen, Sam Okafor and Noor Haddad.

**Suggested reviewers**

- **Ravi Menon:** the only person who has touched all three areas recently, so the best first choice.
- **Alexander Rowe or Sam Okafor** for `time.go`.
- **Mei Chen** for `version7.go`.

**Check before relying on this**

- One commit, `d97a7fa` by Kofi Mensah, is dated 1970-01-01. That date is likely a bad timestamp or a rewritten history, so I would verify that commit.
- Authors appear under several names, for example "Alex Rowe", "Alexander Rowe" and "arowe", and Paul Borman appears as "pborman" and "bormanp". I grouped them by hand, so the counts are approximate.
- Commit emails like `*.harbor.example` and `*.example` look like placeholders, so I wouldn't use them to contact anyone.

